#4471 was marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. The table below is the
same grouping the desk already ships. It is not one cause.

The merge rule is [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject): lowercase
the subject, strip punctuation, merge. Parser reports and hint reports share
those subjects, so they landed in one ticket.

## Two problems

**parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants
(`en-GB`, `de-DE`, and the rest on file) write the day first. Bookings flip:
4 July becomes 7 April. App, email, and booking-v2 form reports are this bug.

**hint.** A different bug. booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field.
People type what the hint says. The form still reads the tenant's day-first
order. Only form reports from alder.physio, copper.studio, and pale.harbour.

Intake's `intakeTag` is a browser guess. It disagrees with tenant cause often
enough that the tag is not the split.

<Callout kind="warn">
Known was wrong. One ticket hid a second bug that needs its own fix.
</Callout>

## What was merged into #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The row that is not this ticket is the hint bug: no ticket of its own. One
GitHub ticket per cause, with the report count the table computes:

- parser → [#1](https://github.com/kosenkobogdan/MEGA.DEV/issues/1)
- hint → [#2](https://github.com/kosenkobogdan/MEGA.DEV/issues/2)

Reports the desk read as a one-day move stay in the parser row, footnoted there.
They are not a third cause in this grouping.

## Engineering · #4471 closed 05 Oct

- parser — **fixed.** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
- hint — **won't fix.** booking-v3 form retired

## Why the merge happened

Triage never reads the body and never asks `causeOf`. During an incident that is
fast. It is also how two date bugs become one known issue.

